// The glasshouse: iron and glass over beds gone wild, lit from inside by what grows there.
//
// In the middle a pillar holds up the night-blooming flower: cling up it to find the Lure,
// and over it to go on.
// Blooms hang low on either side, close enough to swing between. East is the bloom walk.
